# Watcher dies with the wave

If you start `.agents/skills/subagents/watch-agent-context.sh`, kill it in the same turn the last agent you started has reported, or the moment that dispatch is interrupted.

Keep the pid from the background Bash call. `kill` that pid. Done means this session has no `watch-agent-context.sh` process left.

Do not leave a watcher until the 7200s timeout. A watcher with no agent left still spends a later turn on `stopped after 7200s`.
